= BITwiki interdisciplinary content review =

'''Correction: BITwiki is both a general interdisciplinary encyclopedia and a computation-/information-centered knowledge system.''' A subject need not prove independent computational function to warrant inclusion. The former K01 exclusion test and all proposed renames, subordinations and context-only dispositions based exclusively on it are '''withdrawn'''. This was an assistant-introduced editorial interpretation, not an owner-established restriction. See [[BITwiki:Computational scope]].

== Current disposition of the 36 reviewed subjects ==

Retain all 36 existing Core identities subject to normal accuracy, duplication, sourcing and editorial-quality review. Preserve each page's historical provenance, reader depths and semantic relations. Distinct computational methods can be separately represented and linked without replacing legitimate general-science concepts.

