== Useful outcomes retained from prior editorial work ==

* PR #58 improved evidence, references, implementation examples, justified links and [[Resistor]] reading depths. These improvements remain; the policy correction does not revert article text.
* The following Core articles lacked separately authored Simple/Technical presentations in the verified GitHub snapshot: [[Sunk cost effect]], [[Loss aversion]], [[Decoy effect]], [[Status quo bias]]. Add depths only when they improve reader understanding; do not pad for a quota.
* Earth system modeling, computational ecology, plant photoreceptor signaling and biomedical signal processing are possible '''additional''' entries, not compulsory replacements. Confirm nonduplication and reliable subject identity before any creation.
* Audit citation quality, factual precision, reading-depth clarity, semantic edge validity, domain handling and deployment boundaries independently. These are legitimate quality questions, not scope disqualifications.
* The 302-object staging snapshot and previously source-reviewed articles remain subject to further claim-level inspection. Passing the static validator does not certify scientific accuracy.

== Revision and release boundary ==

Earlier PRs #54–#59 introduced or propagated an overly narrow computation-only interpretation. Their contents and the original detailed 36-subject ledger remain recoverable in Git history; they are not binding exclusions after this correction. Source content in <code>Main/</code> is not deleted, moved or renamed by this document. No change to archived V1 sources, production MediaWiki or deployments is authorized.

